	"description": [
		"This anthropology course examines the ocean both as an object of study and as a tool by which to understand social, global, and cultural complexity. Today's economic and geopolitical imaginations are dictated by geographic territorialisms, primarily articulated by political forms such as nation states, area studies, and trenchant regionalisms. The course offers a \"view from the boat\" or an \"oceanic perspective\" to understand contemporary issues such as climate change, border crises, human-non-human relations, and resource extraction, while also expanding our understandings of history, global connection and exchange."
	],
